(Q: How did the integration of carbon into lead-acid battery designs, particularly leading to) Tj
T* (the UltraBattery, address the limitations of conventional VRLA cells and enable their) Tj
T* (suitability for modern utility-scale applications?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0. 0.392 0. rg
56.6929133858267775 189.9214960629919915 Td
(A: Conventional VRLA cells \(GEL/AGM\), while low-maintenance, were limited in their) Tj
T* (ability to operate for extended periods at a partial state of charge \(pSoC\) and handle) Tj
T* (high-rate cycling. The Advanced Lead Acid Battery Consortium \(ALABC\) sponsored) Tj
T* (research that led to carbon-enhanced designs, integrating carbon into the negative) Tj
T* (electrode. This significantly improved the ability of VRLA cells to operate in pSoC, which is) Tj
T* (crucial for grid applications. The UltraBattery, a hybrid of a lead-acid cell and a) Tj
T* (supercapacitor \(with carbon distinct from the negative active material\), further advanced) Tj
T* (this by offering superior power handling, better cell balancing \(e.g., a 32% increase in) Tj
T* (voltage variance over 10 months compared to 140–250% for conventional VRLA controls\),) Tj
T* (and an 'order of magnitude improvement' in cycle life over conventional VRLA, making) Tj
T* (them viable for demanding utility-scale energy storage.) Tj
ET
