(Q: Describe the concept of 'dual purposing' energy storage by combining UPS and grid) Tj
T* (regulation services, detailing how it works, its primary economic advantages, and the) Tj
T* (specific battery characteristic that enables it.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0. 0.392 0. rg
56.6929133858267775 209.7640157480313974 Td
(A: Dual purposing involves combining Uninterruptible Power Supply \(UPS\) functionality) Tj
T* (with grid energy functions, specifically frequency regulation services, to enhance the) Tj
T* (system's business case. It works by installing a slightly larger battery store and operating it) Tj
T* (at a partial State of Charge \(pSoC\), typically around 75% SoC. This allows the battery to) Tj
T* (continuously absorb and supply power for grid regulation when the grid is present, while) Tj
T* (retaining sufficient stored energy to provide UPS support if the grid fails. The primary) Tj
T* (economic advantage is the ability to distribute the system's overheads over multiple) Tj
T* (revenue streams, as the additional cost is primarily just the increase in battery size \(a small) Tj
T* (portion of the total UPS cost\) which is offset by revenue from regulation services. This is) Tj
T* (enabled by advanced VRLA batteries, such as UltraBattery, which are specifically capable) Tj
T* (of operating for extended periods at a partial charge without degradation, unlike) Tj
T* (conventional UPS batteries that are typically kept at 100% charge.) Tj
ET
